    anchor: exactly 1 pixel per motif, color shared across all, appears once per motif
    markers: 3-5 extra-color pixels on bg cells 8-adjacent to skeleton (reference only)
    marker_colors: 2 distinct colors [observed]
    structure: all motifs are distinct dihedral (rot90/flip) variants of the same skeleton+anchor shape
    uniqueness: skeleton+anchor combo must have >=N distinct dihedral variants where N = motif count
    asymmetry: anchor breaks skeleton symmetry so each target has exactly 1 valid alignment
  layout:
    motifs separated by >=4 Manhattan distance
    stamped markers land on bg cells within grid bounds, no overlap with other motifs
  transform:
    find unique dihedral alignment mapping reference skeleton+anchor onto each target
    stamp transformed marker pixels onto target (on bg cells), skeleton unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Design a 4-connected skeleton polyomino (5-6 cells) and place anchor on a bg cell 8-adjacent to it
    2. Verify skeleton+anchor has enough dihedral variants (>=N for N=3-4 motifs)
    3. Place 3-5 marker pixels (2 colors) on bg cells 8-adjacent to skeleton to form the reference patch
    4. Pick N-1 distinct dihedral variants for target motifs; for each, compute transformed marker positions
    5. Choose grid size 13-15 x 13-15; place all motifs (reference + targets) with >=4 Manhattan separation
    6. Verify all transformed marker positions land on bg cells within grid bounds (this is the output)
    7. Remove marker pixels from target motifs to produce the input (targets keep only skeleton+anchor)
